 the chunk proves read-path equivalence and leaves a named deferral for Chunk 2 to close.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:611:**Delivers:** Flow 4 complete (three-layer closed schemas, error mapping with `eventIndex`); Flow 5 complete at event level (skip set, `skipReason`, density of order numbers); Flow 2's recording half (the transaction, `MAX(event_order)` counter, event rows, walk-time result assembly minus messages/turns/work); `listEvents`; closes TC-1.4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:646:Strictly linear, matching the epic's story graph. The two named deferrals (Chunk 1→2: TC-1.4; Chunk 4→5: work-item assertions in TC-3.3/3.6) are the only cross-chunk test debts, both recorded in the chunk that owes them and asserted closed in the chunk that pays them. No chunk mocks a neighbor; the seam between Chunk 4 and 5 is an absent call added later, neither stubbed nor faked.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:652:- Both named deferrals must appear in the receiving story's scope (Story 2: TC-1.4; Story 5: TC-3.3/3.6 work halves) so no story claims completion over a debt it does not own.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:72:  - TC-1.4 deferral to Story 2 recorded as named todo in test file (per spec)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:109:- Story 1: threads domain (newThread file-then-row + compensation, resolve, listThreads, resolveThreadRef single interpreter), registry lazy-create on write only. TC-1.4 deferred to S2.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:110:- Story 2: heaviest, full-staged-risk. Validation precedes idempotency; skips consume no order numbers; key-wins-over-content; dense MAX(event_order). Four arch-risk tests: mid-walk rollback, restart survival, no-lock-on-rejection, system_error rollback parity. Closes TC-1.4. TC-4.4 corru