{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VGMtPNr4NEPWFqRhJ9LGsg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both gates are green. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nTC-1.4 previously **stripped `recordedAt`** before comparing the two read-backs (the comment even said \"modulo recordedAt (wall-clock)\"). That's the weakened assertion the task forbids. The reason it had to strip: the by-id and by-path recordings happen at two different wall-clock instants, so their `recordedAt` values would never match.\n\nThe fix follows the story-local requirement (test-plan: *\"injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`\"*) and the codebase's existing seam convention (`setIntakeWalkHook`).\n\n**Minimal clock path exposed** — `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts`:\n- Added a `setIntakeClock` seam (a module-level `injectedClock`, mirroring the existing `setIntakeWalkHook`).\n- Changed `runMessageEvents`'s clock default to `injectedClock ?? (() => new Date())`. Precedence is explicit-arg > seam > wall clock; production is untouched (`injectedClock` stays null → real wall time). The public `messageEvents(thread, events)` signature is unchanged.\n\n**Exposed through the sanctioned below-SDK seam** — `test/fixtures/intake-seam.ts` and `test/fixtures/index.ts` re-export `setIntakeClock` (fixtures are boundary-check exempt by design).\n\n**TC-1.4 strengthened** — `test/intake.test.ts`:\n- Pins a fixed clock (`setIntakeClock(() => new Date(\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"))`), reset in `afterEach`.\n- Replaced the `strip(...)` comparison with `expect(readById.value).toEqual(readByPath)` — full read-back, **`recordedAt` included, nothing stripped**.\n- Added an assertion that every `recordedAt` equals the injected instant, proving it came from the clock seam rather than wall time.\n\n**Red-manifest** — strengthening a Red-frozen test is a legitimate Red-phase change, so I re-recorded `test/intake.test.ts`'s hash via the sanctioned `scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs` (only that one file). The immutability guard then passes honestly: `test-immutability: OK (7 Red-phase files unchanged)`.\n\n**Gates:**\n- `green-verify` → build, typecheck, lint, boundaries, **49 tests pass**, immutability OK.\n- `verify-all` → including the spawned-binary process suite, **58 tests pass** across 8 files.\n\nThat the full `toEqual` now passes across two independent recordings is itself the proof the seam is wired — under the old wall clock it could not have.\n\nNote: I did not touch `team-impl-log.md`'s receipts (impl-lead-owned process record) since closing TC-1.4's deferral is an acceptance/receipt step, not part of this code change."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":77859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73841117-4412-4191-bf6e-d9dac3fc51d8","uuid":"979c0d2d-5352-4298-b671-c881ac69ec29","request_id":"req_011Cbug2BaFVrbWKDgArNUbt"}
